        "kind": "start",
        "title": "At the gate",
        "description": "The player and Kell walk up to the gate from the sand; the Crakes are leaning on it, about twenty-five feet off. The talking one explains the toll, cheerfully. Let the player answer: pay, haggle, talk, threaten or swing. A fight is the player's choice or the Crakes' answer to an insult or a blow, never the scene's.",
        "cast": {
          "kell": "One dry remark about tolls, then watching the investigator to see what they'll do.",
          "crake-1": "Cheerful, explaining the toll and jingling the cup: a shilling a head.",
          "crake-2": "Leaning on the gate post, silent, cracking his knuckles."
        },
        "lore": []
      }
    },
